From d05b1af7a1b1532b52ab7a0a81a31a6ca6bd4738 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hussain-maker <79055482+Hussain-maker@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:39:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] Keep the player class power bar running when hiding the
 Blizzard player frame

On retail (Midnight) the Blizzard player frame's class power bar also drives
the Personal Resource Display's class resource. XPerl_BlizzFrameDisable
unregistered its events, so combo points shown on the Personal Resource
Display (or moved to the target nameplate by other addons) appeared but
never updated. Leave that bar's events alone; the player frame itself is
still hidden and its other parts are still disabled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 XPerlForever/XPerlForever.lua | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/XPerlForever/XPerlForever.lua b/XPerlForever/XPerlForever.lua
index 228d4d3..ad0ad41 100644
--- a/XPerlForever/XPerlForever.lua
+++ b/XPerlForever/XPerlForever.lua
@@ -1249,8 +1249,10 @@ function XPerl_BlizzFrameDisable(self)
 		debuffFrame:UnregisterAllEvents()
 	end
 
+	-- The player frame's class power bar also drives the Personal Resource Display's class
+	-- resource (e.g. combo points, which other addons can show on the target nameplate).
 	local classPowerBar = self.classPowerBar
-	if classPowerBar then
+	if classPowerBar and self ~= PlayerFrame then
 		classPowerBar:UnregisterAllEvents()
 	end
 
